                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "81da6534-382a-4a7d-b588-aa50470c08e1",
                                "sense_id": "4e496a3f-95d5-30d5-842a-66ae8cb29bc8",
                                "text": "It must here be explained that the tronk, or jail, is the general receptacle, not only of convicted criminals, but of such Hottentots or slaves as are found, improperly or illegally wandering about the country […]",
                                "translation": "在此必须解释的是，tronk，即监狱，是一般的收容所，不仅收容被定罪的罪犯，而且收容那些被发现不正当或非法在国内游荡的霍屯督人或奴隶 […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e80caf62-4ca8-4ce4-955a-fbb079581466",
                                "sense_id": "4e496a3f-95d5-30d5-842a-66ae8cb29bc8",
                                "text": "The diary of another settler, who had been wrongfully imprisoned in the Tronk, and described the daily life there in no uncertain terms […]",
                                "translation": "另一位定居者，他曾被错误地关在监狱里，他在日记里非常清晰地描述了那里的日常生活 […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "09ddc36a-5531-4c4f-9cea-8b4e3b74fe6e",
                                "sense_id": "4e496a3f-95d5-30d5-842a-66ae8cb29bc8",
                                "text": "It was built, as far as I can discover, because the rightly denounced the overcrowding of the old \"tronk\" on the waterfront.",
                                "translation": "据我所知，因为《Cape Argus》报正确地谴责了海滨旧监狱的过度拥挤问题，那里才建了起来。"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
